{
  "name": "Track daily Google search rankings in Google Sheets",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "51a85fa1-c583-4939-b32b-6a510857fd43",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -512,
        256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Track daily Google search rankings in Google Sheets\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Every day, Scrapio searches Google for each of your tracked keywords.\n2. The domain's position in the results is compared against its last logged position.\n3. Every result is appended to Google Sheets, building a full ranking history over time.\n4. A sharp drop (3+ places, or falling out of the results) posts an alert to Slack.\n5. A separate weekly branch reads the sheet and posts a digest of movers to Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Add your Scrapio API credential (get a key at app.scrapio.dev)\n- [ ] Edit the keyword/domain pairs in Set Keywords and Domains\n- [ ] Connect your Google Sheet in both Read nodes and Append Ranking to Sheets (header row: checked_at, keyword, domain, position, url_found, previous_position, position_change)\n- [ ] Add your Slack credential and channel IDs to Send Rank Drop Alert to Slack and Send Weekly Ranking Digest to Slack\n- [ ] Activate the workflow\n\n### Customization tips\n\nAdjust the drop threshold in If Rank Dropped Sharply, or change either schedule."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
